      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "name": "role",
              "value": "devops-engineer",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "value": "=Promote the exact tested images for release {{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }} to UAT — using glab against gitlab-webservice-default.gitlab.svc.cluster.local (project {{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.gitlab_project_path ?? $env.GITLAB_PROJECT_PATH.replace('%2F', '/') }}). Step 1: list merged story MRs targeting `release/{{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }}` (`glab api \"projects/{{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.gitlab_project_path?.replaceAll('/','%2F') ?? $env.GITLAB_PROJECT_PATH }}/merge_requests?target_branch=release/{{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }}&state=merged&labels=type:story\"`). Step 2: for each, fetch its notes (`glab api projects/{{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.gitlab_project_path?.replaceAll('/','%2F') ?? $env.GITLAB_PROJECT_PATH }}/merge_requests/<iid>/notes`) and find QA's comment containing a 'Tested image tags:' block (format `- {service}: v{X}.{Y}.{Z}-rc{N}` per line, one per changed service — see qa-engineer SKILL.md). If a merged story MR has no such comment, STOP and signal n8n blocked with `{\"status\": \"blocked\", \"reason\": \"no tested image tags recorded\", \"mr_iid\": \"<iid>\"}` — never fall back to whatever is currently on SIT, never guess a tag. Step 3: for every {service}:{tag} pair collected across all story MRs, edit `env/uat/{service}/values.yaml` on `main` (create the file if this is the service's first UAT deploy — copy the shape of an existing `env/uat/*/values.yaml` in the repo) setting the image tag field to the exact tag from the comment. Step 4: commit all edited files in one commit (`chore: promote tested images to UAT for {{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }}`) and push to main — ArgoCD's automated syncPolicy on each `{{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.argocd_project ?? $env.ARGOCD_PROJECT }}-<service>-uat` Application picks up the change from there, no image-updater involved (UAT is explicit-sync only). Report which services were updated and to which tags.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "name": "story",
              "value": "={{ $env.RELEASE_VERSION }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
